# English/ASCII machine IDs

Display names (`cityName`, `countryName`, titles, descriptions) **may be localized**.

Machine IDs must **always** be English/ASCII lowercase slugs (or ISO codes). Never store localized script in id fields.

## Fields this applies to

- `cityId` / `city.id`
- `countryId` / `country.id`
- `placeId` and any other `*Id` used as a Firestore key or stable slug
- Trip `from` / `destination` ids, location docs, AI payloads, Cloud Functions responses

## Conventions

- `countryId`: prefer ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 **lowercase** (`sa`, `uz`, `tr`)
- `countryCode`: ISO alpha-2 **uppercase** when present (`SA`)
- `cityId` / `placeId`: lowercase ASCII slug (`makkah`, `prophets-mosque`)
- Reject or re-resolve the sentinel `"unknown"` from `slugifyId` — never persist it when a real place is known

## How to produce ids

- Prefer `resolveEnglishPlaceIds(lat, lon)` or `resolveEnglishPlaceIdsFromAddress(...)` (`language=en`) when the display name may be non-Latin
- Use `countryIdFromParts(name, countryCode)`, `slugifyId(englishName)`, `isAsciiId(value)`
- `isAsciiId` is false for empty values and `"unknown"`

```ts
// ❌ BAD — slugifying Arabic/Cyrillic → "unknown"
cityId: slugifyId(destination.cityName)

// ✅ GOOD — English reverse-geocode (or ISO code) then slug
const ids = await resolveEnglishPlaceIds(lat, lon);
cityId: ids.cityId
countryId: ids.countryId // e.g. "sa"
```

## Cloud Functions / AI

Model prompts must require: localized display strings OK; `placeId` / `cityId` / `countryId` / `countryCode` English/ASCII only. Validate before writing to Firestore.
